    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i run a small online stationery shop in lyon and im trying to make sure i'm following gdpr rules correctly before my audit next month. i mostly just collect customer names, email addresses, and shipping addresses for orders. can u give me a quick summary of the main principles i need to follow for those kinds of things?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! Under GDPR, you'll need to ensure that you have a legitimate reason for collecting and processing customer data, you gain clear consent for this purpose, and you keep it secure. Consider providing a clear privacy notice to customers, explaining what data you collect, why you need it, and how it will be protected. Remember to let customers know they can access, rectify, or delete their data upon request. Also, never sell personal data without explicit permission. Regularly reviewing your practices against GDPR requirements will help maintain compliance. Do you need help with a specific section or privacy notice?",
