    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i'm mostly worried about the \"security\" part. like, i dont have a dedicated IT team or anything, i just use a basic ecommerce platform and an email list. what are the actual practical steps i should take to make sure my customers' info isn't being accessed by people they didn't authorize? also, what should i do if i realize data was leaked?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To secure customer data, you should use strong, unique passwords for all interfaces, keep software updated, especially within your e-commerce platform, and enable any encryption or security features provided. Back up data regularly. Limit access to sensitive information, and you don’t need a large IT team for this—basic digital best practices are sufficient. If data appears to be leaked, act quickly: notify customers, GDPR regulators, and offer support to affected individuals. Document what happened and how you’re addressing the issue, as you should report this breach within 72 hours, as required by GDPR. Would you like me to provide a list of good practices or perhaps a template for notifying customers of a breach?",
